# OKF and repository-governance edits

- Read `AGENTS.md` and the relevant current documents under `docs/` before editing.
- Treat `docs/` as an OKF v0.2 bundle.
- Ordinary concept documents require YAML frontmatter with a non-empty `type`.
- Non-root `index.md` files are frontmatter-free navigation; `docs/index.md` is the bundle-root exception.
- Preserve one natural current owner for each durable rule; prefer links over duplicated summaries.
- Keep phase records historical and canonical knowledge current.
- Check affected indexes and cross-links after renames, moves, supersession, or new knowledge.
- Do not add `status`, `stale_after`, timestamps, or other metadata mechanically; use lifecycle/freshness metadata only when it carries real maintenance value.
- If current documentation is stale, update or supersede it rather than coding around it.
- Do not create extra audit/report files when the finding belongs in an existing owner or phase record.
- Preserve the lifecycle boundary: `000–011` concept design, `012` pre-implementation preparation, then a separate downstream engineering lifecycle.
- Agent adapters must remain thin; shared policy belongs in `AGENTS.md` and `docs/methodology/agentic-development-governance.md`.
